{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Hecke.MarkovBondFactor","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovBondFactor","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Hecke.MarkovTrace","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Abel"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovTrace.trace_bond_pair_factorizes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovTrace.trace_bond_pair_factorizes","kind":"theorem","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovBondFactor.lean#L135-L157","doc":"**Two-bond factorization.**  For bridge crossings at generators\n`i < j` the Markov trace factorizes over the bonds:\n`tr_M((c₁σ_i + d₁)(c₂σ_j + d₂)) = (c₁z + d₁)(c₂z + d₂)`.\nThis is the `A = 3` (two-bond chain) instance of\n`tr_atom = tr_free · ∏ f_bond`; uses `trace_prod_gen`\n(`tr_M(σ_iσ_j) = z²`, two Markov peels). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovTrace.trace_bond_crossing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovTrace.trace_bond_crossing","kind":"theorem","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovBondFactor.lean#L125-L133","doc":"**Per-bond trace factor (one bond).**  The Markov trace of a bridge\ncrossing `c • σ_i + d • 1` is its conditional expectation\n`c · z + d` — the fibre-level form of the per-bond binding factor\n`f_bond(q)`:  `f_pp = z` (`(c,d) = (1,0)`), `f_nn = z − h`\n(`(1, −h)`), `f_pn = z − h(½ − δ/4)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}